{"path":"experimental/fs/remove","title":"std::experimental::filesystem::remove, std::experimental::filesystem::remove_all","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::filesystem::</span>remove, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::filesystem::</span>remove_all","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/fs/remove","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"On POSIX systems, this function typically calls unlink and rmdir as needed, on Windows RemoveDirectoryW and DeleteFileW.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/filesystem\">&lt;experimental/filesystem&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> remove<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> remove<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p, error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a> remove_all<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a> remove_all<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p, error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> The file or empty directory identified by the path <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> is deleted as if by the POSIX <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/remove.html\" data-external=\"1\">remove</a>. Symlinks are not followed (symlink is removed, not its target).</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Deletes the contents of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> (if it is a directory) and the contents of all its subdirectories, recursively, then deletes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> itself as if by repeatedly applying the POSIX <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/remove.html\" data-external=\"1\">remove</a>. Symlinks are not followed (symlink is removed, not its target).</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> path to delete\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ec\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> out-parameter for error reporting in the non-throwing overload\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> if the file was deleted, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> if it did not exist. The overload that takes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> argument returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> on errors.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Returns the number of files and directories that were deleted (which may be zero if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> did not exist to begin with). The overload that takes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> argument returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">static_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> on error.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\nThe overload that does not take an <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter throws <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/filesystem_error\">filesystem_error</a> on underlying OS API errors, constructed with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> as the first argument and the OS error code as the error code argument. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\"><span class=\"kw698\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bad_alloc</span></span></a></span></code> may be thrown if memory allocation fails. The overload taking an <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter sets it to the OS API error code if an OS API call fails, and executes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ec.<span class=\"me1\">clear</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> if no errors occur. This overload has <div class=\"t-noexcept-inline\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\"><code>noexcept</code></a> specification:&nbsp;&nbsp;<div class=\"t-noexcept-box\"><span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span></span></span></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>On POSIX systems, this function typically calls <code>unlink</code> and <code>rmdir</code> as needed, on Windows <code>RemoveDirectoryW</code> and <code>DeleteFileW</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdint&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;experimental/filesystem&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> fs <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span> dir <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">temp_directory_path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">create_directories</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>dir <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"abcdef/example\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a> n <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">remove_all</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>dir <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"abcdef\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Deleted \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" files or directories<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Deleted 2 files or directories</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/remove\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>remove</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  erases a file <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/fs","title":"Filesystem library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::filesystem::remove, std::experimental::filesystem::remove_all","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. The file or empty directory identified by the path p is deleted as if by the POSIX remove."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"p, ec"},{"label":"Return value","note":"true if the file was deleted, false if it did not exist. The overload that takes error_code& argument returns false on errors."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"The overload that does not take an"},{"label":"Notes","note":"On POSIX systems, this function typically calls unlink and rmdir as needed, on Windows RemoveDirectoryW and DeleteFileW."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"remove","note":"erases a file"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":326,"codeBlockCount":2}
